B = [
('Heinz','North America','1900s-present','food','In the style of Heinz, heritage American label design built on a keystone-shaped emblem. A pointed arched cream panel with a fine tomato-red outline and a bold central shield holds ornate white and cream serif capitals set on a gentle curve, with small banner ribbons, an established-year line and tiny fine print. Palette is tomato red, warm cream, antique gold and deep navy, with a vivid mustard yellow or leaf green accent for variants. Surfaces are glossy printed paper, tinted glass and enamel with crisp thin keylines. Layouts are tidy, symmetrical and centred, with repeat patterns of small keystone outlines on solid red fields. Lettering is proud, slightly antique and wholesome.'),
('Campbell','North America','1900s-present','food','In the style of Campbell, flat, symmetrical, uniform and instantly legible. A bold red upper field meets a clean white lower field with a thin gold line between them, and a round gold medallion seal with a fine embossed ring sits dead centre. The main wordmark is a thin, flowing, connected red script, supported by small white sans-serif capitals on the red. Colour is applied in broad flat blocks with no gradients, in red, white and gold, with occasional pastel or deep green variations of the same layout. Finish is satin printed metal and smooth coated paper, with identical elements repeated in tidy grids. Mood is dependable, nostalgic, plain and quietly pop-art.'),
('Tabasco','North America','1900s-present','food','In the style of Tabasco, fiery red and deep green heritage built around a diamond-shaped emblem. A bold red diamond with a white inner outline and wide white serif capitals sits flanked by green oval bands and a thin gold or white border. Patterns repeat diamonds and fine lines edge to edge in dense tiles. Palette is hot red, forest green, cream and gold, with bright orange, yellow and teal used as colour-coded variant accents. Surfaces are glossy enamel, tinted glass and crisp printed paper with a vintage stamp feel. Lettering is sturdy, tightly spaced capitals with fine outline text curving around the edge. Mood is spicy, authentic, Southern and bold, with an oversized wordmark cropped at the edges.'),
('Marmite','Europe','1920s-present','food','In the style of Marmite, blunt, cheeky two-tone design. Thick glossy near-black surfaces contrast with a bright sunshine yellow field, with a red oval or ribbon label and a tiny union-flag-like accent. Chunky white or yellow serif capitals with a heavy slab feel arch across the label, above a small ornamental crest. Forms are squat, rounded, heavy and soft-cornered, with ridged shoulders and a plain broad base. Palette is near-black, yellow, signal red, green and white, with gold foil in luxury variants and playful colour swaps in limited editions. Finish is high gloss with sharp highlights. Mood is plain, confident, humorous and polarising yet proud.'),
('Hershey','North America','1900s-present','confectionery','In the style of Hershey, sturdy, warm American chocolate-brown design. Deep glossy chocolate-brown fields carry bold white or silver condensed slab-like capitals in a straight horizontal wordmark, underlined by a thin curved swoosh. Flat colour accents in red, gold, orange, purple or blue distinguish variants against the dark brown base. Surfaces include silver metallic foil, satin paper wrap, raised square grid embossing and rounded rectangle panels. A teardrop silhouette with a small flat base and rounded peak recurs as an emblem. Patterns use repeated tiny wordmarks and bold diagonal ribbons. Mood is honest, nostalgic, generous and unfussy, with playful bright illustrated variants.'),
('Nescafe','Europe','1960s-present','beverages','In the style of Nescafe, bold red and white with a warm coffee-brown depth. A solid signal red field carries a white rounded wordmark with a slim outline and a small oval or shield badge. Forms are rounded, cylindrical and soft-edged, with a clear tinted window revealing a warm brown interior. Palette is red, white, cream, coffee brown and gold, with dark charcoal for premium lines and deep green and tan for earthy variants. Surfaces are glossy lacquer, matt paper, foil film and cork-like textures. Decorative patterns use curling steam lines, bean shapes and hand-drawn leaf motifs in repeating tiles. Mood is friendly, reassuring, bright and morning-fresh, with crisp blocks of colour.'),
('Kikkoman','East Asia','1960s-present','food','In the style of Kikkoman, precise, balanced, restrained Japanese practicality. A bold red and black hexagonal crest with a stylised white mark sits on plain white or black fields with generous empty space. Forms are slender, softly faceted and gently tapered, with small glossy red cone accents. Materials are clear glass with dark amber depth, glossy black enamel, matt white ceramic and clean paper labels with fine hairline rules. Palette is deep red, black, white, amber and soft cream, with small bright yellow or green accents for variants. Lettering is clean, wide sans-serif capitals with small Japanese brush characters beside it. Mood is calm, minimal, ergonomic and modern-traditional.'),
('Milo','Oceania','1960s-present','beverages','In the style of Milo, energetic, vivid green wholesome design. Saturated apple green covers broad surfaces, set against deep forest green, white and warm chocolate brown. A bold chunky rounded wordmark in white with a dark outline and a slim banner sits on a green block, with a small red or yellow burst accent. Surfaces are glossy ridged metal, matt printed card and soft-touch plastic, with a stylised ribbon curve wrapping around shapes. Patterns use dynamic diagonal slashes, dotted energy sparks, hexagon cells and simple sporty line illustrations. Forms are rounded, cylindrical and sturdy with bevelled ribs. Mood is optimistic, active and playful, with strong green dominance.'),
('Bang & Olufsen','Europe','1960s-present','electronics','In the style of Bang & Olufsen, serene, sculptural Scandinavian luxury. Forms are slim, tall, softly geometric and minimalist, with tapering cones, pyramids and thin floating plates. Materials are anodised and brushed aluminium, finely perforated metal mesh in tiny repeating patterns, polished black glass, oiled oak, dark walnut, wool fabric in charcoal and warm grey, and soft natural tan leather. Edges are razor sharp with tiny even gaps and hairline seams, with large circular elements and delicate pearl-blasted textures. Palette is silver, graphite, black, natural wood and muted earthy tones such as sand, terracotta and sage. Lettering is tiny, thin, lowercase and widely spaced. Mood is calm, quiet and understated.'),
('Leica','Europe','1930s-present','cameras','In the style of Leica, understated, precise, timeless German craft. A small round red dot emblem with a white handwritten script wordmark is the single accent against black. Surfaces are matt black enamel, polished and brushed silver chrome, finely pebbled black leather-like texture and brass showing through at worn edges. Compact rectangular forms have flat planes and crisp edges, with fine knurled bands, engraved white numerals and thin white sans-serif capitals. Palette is black, silver, signal red and white, with occasional olive, tan or red leather accents. Minimal, free of clutter, with perfectly even gaps and honest patina. Mood is quiet, confident and meticulous.'),
]
